  </work>
  <identification>
    <creator type="composer">Anonymous · Playford 1705</creator>
    <rights>Anonymous, Greensleeves to a Ground with Division; complete fifteen divisions from the 1705 fourth edition of Playford's Division Violin, second part; typeset by Allen Garvin, Mutopia-2009/12/15-1730, Public Domain. Music Viewer complete violin/piano adaptation: all fifteen source divisions, all source pitches, slurs and each original volta 2 retained; the first three implicit notes of division 5 are explicitly notated as quarters, correcting the source's inherited dotted halves which overfill its first 3/2 measure. The source's own eight-measure ground bass accompanies each division on a piano bass staff. No extra harmony is added. Source half-note=80, quarter-note=160.</rights>
  </identification>
